mike-sdk: quick question for the SDK team: do we auto-install undici for Node users or rely on global fetch + docs? thinking about edge bundle size and DX.

olga-ux: strong preference: do NOT auto-bundle. Edge-first apps must keep tiny bundles. docs + a clear error + an opt-in install is better UX than surprising bundles.

raj-plat: agrees with olga. technical sketch: export a small sync helper for require() users and an async ensureFetch() for ESM. that allows CJS consumers to detect at startup without top-level await.

sam-eng: rough example we can ship (ESM + CJS friendly):

```js
// lib/fetch-fallback.mjs (ESM entry)
export function getFetchSync() {
  return typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function' ? globalThis.fetch : null;
}

export async function ensureFetch() {
  const f = getFetchSync();
  if (f) return f;
  const m = await import('undici');
  return m.fetch;
}
```

mike-sdk: nice. for CJS we add a tiny require shim that exposes the same API but without top-level await. consumers call ensureFetch().then(...).

raj-plat: typings gotcha: if we reference RequestInit or Response directly consumers without "DOM" lib will error. propose shipping a minimal types file like "fetch-types.d.ts" and re-exporting a Fetch type in our public types.

olga-ux: +1. please document the two UX paths: edge-first (no undici) and node-first (install undici). include a copy/paste tsconfig snippet for folks who want to add DOM lib.

ci-bot: CI checklist: add matrix jobs for Node 16/18/20, Bun, and a Workers runtime (miniflare). Run the basic request/streaming tests under each.

sam-eng: about retries/auth: we'll implement a high-level retry wrapper that sits above fetch so token refresh and idempotent retry logic is identical across runtimes. underlying pool tuning (undici Agent) remains optional config.

mike-sdk: packaging note: mark undici as optionalDependency or document "npm i undici" for Node <20. optionalDependency still fetches on npm install though; maybe list it as optionalPeerDependency? pros/cons in the package.json PR.

raj-plat: suggest optionalDependency + docs showing how to avoid installing it in edge-only projects (pnpm flags, bundle config). add examples for Next.js Edge vs Server.

olga-ux: also add a FAQ entry: "If you see TS errors about RequestInit" with two fixes: add DOM lib or import our fetch-types. that will cut down on support tickets.

sam-eng: action items: 1) implement fetch-fallback + CJS shim (sam), 2) add minimal fetch-types.d.ts and re-export (raj), 3) update README with Next.js/Vite/webpack notes (olga), 4) CI matrix (ci-bot + raj). I'll open the PR by EOD and tag reviewers.

mike-sdk: sounds good. let's avoid any surprises in edge builds — no implicit polyfills. thanks.
